DATA = " IDs at backend boundary too; bounded Unicode secrets, reject NUL and oversize blobs according to CredMan generic 2560-byte limit. Use UTF-16LE credential blobs consistent with documented Cred APIs. Protect process invocation: static `powershell.exe` + `-EncodedCommand` string built exclusively from a fixed source constant, `shell:false`, `windowsHide:true`, JSON input on stdin, capped output and input, force termination on timeout and output overflow. Use `Add-Type` fixed C# code with P/Invoke layouts correct for Windows x64/arm64, `CredFree` on reads, native error handling; emit JSON protocol result with no secret in diagnostics. `available()` must execute a non-writing capability check (at least validate helper execution and API entry points) rather than blindly returning true. No missing-key signal may be mistaken for a general native failure. Never reuse profile IDs as file names for new storage.\n\nKeep existing `RetiredWindowsSecretCleanupBackend` compatibility path only as an explicitly isolated delete operation after successful OS credential deletion; legacy path remains ID-derived only for preexisting retired blobs, not as new storage. Deleting old metadata must work when no CredMan entry exists. Preserve same-service mutation queue and rollback on metadata write failures; note that separate daemon instances do not have transactional metadata coordination. Do not delete unrelated profiles, do not silently downgrade billing. Tests should mock the isolated native command boundary (not pretend to test Windows OS on Linux) and cover set/get/update/delete, two independent IDs, hostile IDs, Unicode, missing/error/timeout, cancellation, status, metadata failure rollback, legacy cleanup, Settings and BYOK run no-cloud-fallback tests where executable. Native Windows tests must explicitly be NOT_RUN if no Windows host.\n\n## Adversarial self-review, corrections and freeze\n1. **PowerShell stdout / command-line leak:** naive invocation interpolates secret into `-Command` and PowerShell errors echo inputs. Correction: fixed encoded command, JSON stdin only, sanitized errors, bounded stdout, disable profile, do not log raw child streams.\n2. **Incorrect CredRead memory ownership / Unicode:** naive unmanaged P/Invoke can truncate Unicode or leak freed memory. Correction: aligned CREDENTIAL layout, UTF-16LE bytes and explicit length, copy before `CredFree`; reject limits and NUL; test Unicode round trip through mocked protocol and mark native ABI unverified.\n3. **Incorrect capability status:** checking for `powershell.exe` alone could show success despite blocked Add-Type/Cred APIs. Correction: run a safe native `probe` action that compiles/imports required APIs without writing a credential; propagate failure from save regardless of status.\n4. **Concurrent updates / cross-profile loss:** a single-file vault or delete-and-recreate CredMan scheme can overwrite other profiles. Correction: independent OS targets, make `CredWriteW` replace only target; preserve daemon metadata mutation queue; document cross-process metadata atomicity limitation.\n5. **Legacy compatibility:** dropping retired file deletion silently changes old delete semantics. Correction: retain legacy cleanup exclusively for delete, validate ID, and test; do not confuse its old path with newly introduced secure file storage.\n6. **PowerShell child hangs:** helper can block forever on enterprise policy prompts or stdin. Correction: enforce deadlines and bounded pipes; fail closed, never claim success after timeout.\n\nFrozen before changes to repository source. This is a self-critique, not an independent audit. No historical patches, scanner issues or CodeQL findings used.\n"
